        "title": "feat(ui): redesign chat composer controls",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- redesign the Control UI chat composer around a compact model/provider picker with reasoning and speed controls\n- combine chat and voice options under Settings, move attachment/camera controls, and switch the primary action between microphone, stop, and send states\n- add responsive desktop/mobile layout, five-line input growth, sender-aligned message bubbles, context/progress indicators, and scoped model-catalog compatibility handling\n\n## Behavioral proof\n\nCaptured from the real Control UI page using the repository E2E mock Gateway.\n\n### Before\n\n<!-- BEFORE_SCREENSHOT -->\n\n<!-- BEFORE_VIDEO -->\n\n### After\n\n<!-- AFTER_SCREENSHOT -->\n\n<!-- AFTER_MODEL_PICKER -->\n\n<!-- AFTER_SETTINGS -->\n\n<!-- AFTER_DESKTOP_VIDEO -->\n\n<!-- AFTER_MOBILE_SCREENSHOT -->\n\n<!-- AFTER_MOBILE_VIDEO -->\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui.config.ts --configLoader runner` (2,059 tests)\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts --configLoader runner ui/src/e2e/chat-composer-redesign.e2e.test.ts ui/src/e2e/browser-talk-start-stop.e2e.test.ts` (6 tests)\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:check`\n- `pnpm --dir ui build`\n- `$autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main` (clean)\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: Control UI chat composer layout, provider/model selection, reasoning and speed controls, combined chat/voice settings, attachments, mobile camera capture, voice start/stop, send-state switching, context/progress display, and message alignment.\n\nReal environment tested: Real Control UI page in Chromium at 1920x1080 desktop and 393x852 mobile, backed by the repository E2E mock Gateway.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch: Opened Chat, selected providers/models, changed reasoning and speed, opened Settings, exercised five-line overflow, started and stopped voice capture, verified microphone-to-send switching, opened mobile camera capture, and attached the captured image.\n\nEvidence after fix: Before/after screenshots plus desktop and mobile WebM recordings attached above.\n\nObserved result after fix: The composer remains compact and centered on full desktop, exposes model/reasoning/speed controls, preserves scoped model catalogs, limits text growth to five lines, switches voice/send/stop actions correctly, and attaches mobile camera images.\n\nWhat was not tested: Physical mobile camera hardware and a live external voice provider; browser media and Gateway responses were deterministic fixtures.\n\n## Release note\n\nRedesigns the Control UI chat composer with integrated model, reasoning, speed, settings, attachment, camera, and voice controls across desktop and mobile.\n",
